    {
      "id": "B01",
      "title": "Normal enabled-autocorrection commit has no exact spelling/caret guarantee",
      "reason": "Case 8 commits an invented word with space while all normal plain features, including autocorrection and replacements, remain enabled. The frozen contract neither names a lexicon nor guarantees those words survive a normal boundary commit unchanged. The full literal text/caret at step 2 and subsequent dependent text are internally arithmetically consistent but cannot be validated as the uniquely required behavior. This also prevents admission of the positive learning control as written.",
      "resolution": "Reject the unproved oracle. Obtain an independent contract-only deterministic normal commit rule before choosing an oracle; do not infer it from implementation, smoke, calibration, baseline, or candidate behavior.",
