    {
      "id": "B02",
      "title": "Exact normal dictionary count and total-count units are unspecified",
      "reason": "The contract requires real fresh-stack readbacks and normal positive controls, but does not define count increment, aggregation, token normalization, or bilingual total-count semantics. Case 8 assumes exactly one for both the named word and total after one normal commit in each of en_US, es and en_es. Positive touch learning is a contract-supported control intent; the exact integer values are an unadmitted semantic assumption, explicitly acknowledged in authorship. Private absence and unchanged existing counts are sound policy requirements once a valid normal readback is established.",
      "resolution": "Reject exact 1 readbacks pending a pre-reveal contract-only rule. Do not change expectations to observed implementation values. The schema offers no positive-integer predicate for dictionary counts.",
