    {
      "id": "B03",
      "title": "Captured stale-choice refusal is not specified",
      "reason": "The schema defines capture of an offered real choice and choose of that captured choice, with explicit failure on missing capture. It does not state an identity/context binding rule, stale-choice rejection behavior, or a rule that a previously offered literal choice is discarded after a private-field transition. Privacy disabling predictions does not by itself uniquely specify how an explicitly chosen stored literal behaves. Cases 12 and 13 require a no-op choose after host replacement, and their following inserts rely on unchanged selection. Those are plausible requirements but are not uniquely derivable from this frozen contract.",
      "resolution": "Reject both no-op choose oracles rather than guessing stale-choice semantics. Any admitted rule must be specified independently before reveal. Runtime capture must still select an actually offered matching kind/text, retain its actual identity, fail explicitly when absent, and never manufacture a choice.",
