    {
      "id": "B04",
      "title": "Private-origin permanence after return to normal is unspecified without invalidation",
      "reason": "Case 18 captures in private then switches to normal without invalidateGuard. The contract requires nonprivate, matching stable ID/contexts, no selection and no invalidation; it explicitly makes caller invalidation persistent. It does not unambiguously specify whether origin privacy itself permanently disqualifies that guard after current traits become normal. The assumed refusal at steps 2 and 3 is therefore not validated. If the opposite interpretation permitted core insertion, the single shared document oracle would also diverge from unavailable native automatic. Steps 4 through 6 inherit the unproved document state until the host reset at step 7. Case 16 explicitly invalidates and is unaffected.",
      "resolution": "Reject this permanence expectation pending a contract-only origin-versus-current privacy definition. Do not add an invalidateGuard silently, because that would change the challenge.",
