      "title": "Apostrophe in type is outside the declared letter-tap semantics",
      "reason": "Case 15 step 1 in every language sends an ASCII apostrophe through type. The schema describes type as keywise letters with centered taps and spaces via insertSpace; literal nonletters are explicitly available through insert. No punctuation tap or fallback behavior for type is declared. The JSON shape is valid and ideal literal UTF16 arithmetic is correct, but this payload is semantically unadmitted under the stated capabilities. Steps 2 through 6 depend on it; host at step 7 resets the document.",
      "resolution": "Reject the undeclared operation behavior. A pre-reveal rewrite could explicitly use the already-declared literal insert operation for punctuation with retained intermediate full oracles, but splitting operations would be a substantive scenario edit; no correction is fabricated here.",
